's certificate of trust differ from the UTC model?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Minnesota's statute is executed by the settlor or trustee rather than only by trustees, and it requires the signature to be under oath before a notary public. The statute also has specific subdivisions for real property transactions that require identification of each settlor and each original trustee and a standard authorization statement. The certificate must state that no other provisions limit trustee powers, and amendment or revocation is only effective as to a party upon actual notice."}}]})} />
